#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:355
msgid ""
"The rest of these methods below come in just before the terminating "
"`.argv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:357
msgid ".alias(key, alias)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:360
msgid ""
"Set key names as equivalent such that updates to a key will propagate to "
"aliases and vice-versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:363
msgid ""
"Optionally `.alias()` can take an object that maps keys to aliases. Each "
"key of this object should be the canonical version of the option, and "
"each value should be a string or an array of strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:367
msgid ".default(key, value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:370
msgid "Set `argv[key]` to `value` if no option was specified on `process.argv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:372
msgid ""
"Optionally `.default()` can take an object that maps keys to default "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:374
msgid ".demand(key, [msg | boolean])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:376
msgid ".require(key, [msg | boolean])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:378
msgid ".required(key, [msg | boolean])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:381
msgid ""
"If `key` is a string, show the usage information and exit if `key` wasn't"
" specified in `process.argv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:384
msgid ""
"If `key` is a number, demand at least as many non-option arguments, which"
" show up in `argv._`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:387
msgid "If `key` is an Array, demand each element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:389
msgid ""
"If a `msg` string is given, it will be printed when the argument is "
"missing, instead of the standard error message. This is especially "
"helpful for the non-option arguments in `argv._`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:392
msgid ""
"If a `boolean` value is given, it controls whether the option is "
"demanded; this is useful when using `.options()` to specify command line "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:395
msgid ".requiresArg(key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:398
msgid ""
"Specifies either a single option key (string), or an array of options "
"that must be followed by option values. If any option value is missing, "
"show the usage information and exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:402
msgid ""
"The default behaviour is to set the value of any key not followed by an "
"option value to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:405
msgid ".implies(x, y)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:408
msgid "Given the key `x` is set, it is required that the key `y` is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:410
msgid "implies can also accept an object specifying multiple implications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:412
msgid ".describe(key, desc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:415
msgid "Describe a `key` for the generated usage information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:417
msgid ""
"Optionally `.describe()` can take an object that maps keys to "
"descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:419
msgid ".option(key, opt)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:421
msgid ".options(key, opt)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:424
msgid ""
"Instead of chaining together "
"`.alias().demand().default().describe().string()`, you can specify keys "
"in `opt` for each of the chainable methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:427
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:442
msgid "is the same as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:452
msgid ""
"Optionally `.options()` can take an object that maps keys to `opt` "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:469
msgid ".usage(message, opts)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:472
msgid ""
"Set a usage message to show which commands to use. Inside `message`, the "
"string `$0` will get interpolated to the current script name or node "
"command for the present script similar to how `$0` works in bash or perl."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:476
msgid "`opts` is optional and acts like calling `.options(opts)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:478
msgid ".example(cmd, desc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:481
msgid ""
"Give some example invocations of your program. Inside `cmd`, the string "
"`$0` will get interpolated to the current script name or node command for"
" the present script similar to how `$0` works in bash or perl. Examples "
"will be printed out as part of the help message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:486
msgid ".check(fn)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:489
msgid "Check that certain conditions are met in the provided arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:491
msgid ""
"`fn` is called with two arguments, the parsed `argv` hash and an array of"
" options and their aliases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:493
msgid ""
"If `fn` throws or returns `false`, show the thrown error, usage "
"information, and exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:496
msgid ".fail(fn)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:499
msgid ""
"Method to execute when a failure occurs, rather then printing the failure"
" message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:501
msgid "`fn` is called with the failure message that would have been printed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:503
msgid ".boolean(key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:506
msgid ""
"Interpret `key` as a boolean. If a non-flag option follows `key` in "
"`process.argv`, that string won't get set as the value of `key`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:509
msgid ""
"`key` will default to `false`, unless an `default(key, undefined)` is "
"explicitly set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:512
msgid "If `key` is an Array, interpret all the elements as booleans."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:514
msgid ".string(key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:517
msgid ""
"Tell the parser logic not to interpret `key` as a number or boolean. This"
" can be useful if you need to preserve leading zeros in an input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:520
msgid "If `key` is an Array, interpret all the elements as strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:522
msgid ""
"`.string('_')` will result in non-hyphenated arguments being interpreted "
"as strings, regardless of whether they resemble numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:525
msgid ".config(key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:528
msgid ""
"Tells the parser to interpret `key` as a path to a JSON config file. The "
"file is loaded and parsed, and its properties are set as arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:531
msgid ".wrap(columns)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:534
msgid "Format usage output to wrap at `columns` many columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:536
msgid ".strict()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:539
msgid ""
"Any command-line argument given that is not demanded, or does not have a "
"corresponding description, will be reported as an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:542
msgid ".help([option, [description]])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:545
msgid ""
"Add an option (e.g., `--help`) that displays the usage string and exits "
"the process. If present, the `description` parameter customises the "
"description of the help option in the usage string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:549
msgid "If invoked without parameters, `.help` returns the generated usage string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:551 ../../source/yargs_README.md:603
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:559 ../../source/yargs_README.md:611
msgid "Later on, ```argv``` can be retrived with ```yargs.argv```"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:561
msgid ".version(version, option, [description])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:564
msgid ""
"Add an option (e.g., `--version`) that displays the version number (given"
" by the `version` parameter) and exits the process. If present, the "
"`description` parameter customises the description of the version option "
"in the usage string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:568
msgid ".showHelpOnFail(enable, [message])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:571
msgid ""
"By default, yargs outputs a usage string if any error is detected. Use "
"the `.showHelpOnFail` method to customize this behaviour. if `enable` is "
"`false`, the usage string is not output. If the `message` parameter is "
"present, this message is output after the error message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:598
msgid ".showHelp(fn=console.error)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:601
msgid "Print the usage data using `fn` for printing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:613
msgid ".exitProcess(enable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:616
msgid ""
"By default, yargs exits the process when the user passes a help flag, "
"uses the `.version` functionality or when validation fails. Calling "
"`.exitProcess(false)` disables this behavior, enabling further actions "
"after yargs have been validated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:618
msgid ".parse(args)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:621
msgid "Parse `args` instead of `process.argv`. Returns the `argv` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:623
msgid ".argv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:626
msgid "Get the arguments as a plain old object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:628
msgid "Arguments without a corresponding flag show up in the `argv._` array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/yargs_README.md:630
msgid ""
"The script name or node command is available at `argv.$0` similarly to "
"how `$0` works in bash or perl."
msgstr ""

